{number: 95}
{title: O Jesus, I Have Promised}
{key: C}

{start_of_verse: 1}
O [C] Jesus, I have [F] promised to [C] serve Thee to the [G7] end;
Be [C] Thou forever [F] near me, my [C] Master [G7] and my [C] Friend:
I [G7] shall not fear the [C] battle if [F] Thou art by my [G7] side,
Nor [C] wander from the [F] pathway if [C] Thou wilt [G7] be my [C] Guide.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 2}
O [C] let me feel Thee [F] near me; the [C] world is ever [G7] near;
I [C] see the sights that [F] dazzle, the [C] tempting [G7] sounds I [C] hear;
My [G7] foes are ever [C] near me, a-[F] round me and with-[G7] in;
But, [C] Jesus, draw Thou [F] nearer, and [C] shield my [G7] soul from [C] sin.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
O [C] Jesus, Thou hast [F] promised to [C] all who follow [G7] Thee,
That [C] where Thou art in [F] glory there [C] shall Thy [G7] servant [C] be;
And, [G7] Jesus, I have [C] promised to [F] serve Thee to the [G7] end;
O [C] give me grace to [F] follow, my [C] Master [G7] and my [C] Friend.
{end_of_verse}
